# Build-A-Tower — art & vision

Scope: **this project only**. Do not apply these preferences to other Escape work or global Cursor sessions.

## Current slice

Stay on the 2D height×width grid and placeholder cells unless the user explicitly asks to advance visual/tech slices.

## Art polish (when assets are made)

Target the polish of high-end stylized building packs (bright teal / orange / cream / stone; soft gradients; crisp edge highlights; readable materials; no heavy black outlines). Prefer side-cutaway room modules with that finish — not isometric whole-building silhouettes as the primary tower view.

## Mid-term look (2.5D cutaway)

Evolve toward a Project Highrise–style orthographic cutaway: rooms as depth boxes (floor slabs, back/side walls, interiors), tiered tower silhouette, parallax on background / depth layers for a 3D feel — still driven by the 2D grid until a true 3D build is requested.

## Long-term product (true 3D)

A later 3D (or separate 3D) version may add depth as a build axis (H×W×D block placement), freer room footprints, richer elevator/stair routing, and translucent / transparent layering so players can slice and dive into zones to build, rebuild, manage, and upgrade. Do not implement that model until asked; keep Slice #1 architecture compatible where cheap (clear floor/cell concepts), but do not prematurely invent a voxel API.
